  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $6$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n6=\\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{5}$ is $\\frac{5}{3}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n6÷\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{6}{1}÷\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{3}=\\frac{6\\times 5}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{30}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n30÷3=10\n$$",
